# AAI canonical `docs/ai/` inventory — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the
# docs-audit `docs_ai_noncanon` class (CHANGE docs-ai-canon).
#
# CONTRACT
# - One entry per line: an allowed DIRECT child of `docs/ai/` (a directory or a
#   file). Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Read by
#   .aai/scripts/lib/docs-audit-core.mjs (loadDocsAiCanon); an ABSENT or empty
#   list disables the class entirely — a repo that has not synced this file is
#   never flagged.
# - EXACT names only — no globs, no patterns. Temp/aside/scratch files have no
#   canonical home under docs/ai (they belong in a real scratch dir outside the
#   governed tree), so there is deliberately no dot-tempfile escape hatch.
# - Vendored and resynced: never add a project-specific name here. A target
#   project extends the set via `docs_ai_canon_extra:` in
#   docs/ai/docs-audit.yaml (project-owned, survives an /aai-update).
# - WHY THIS EXISTS: downstream agents invented `docs/ai/validation/` and
#   `docs/ai/hitl/` in two days. Both leaked as untracked noise / mislocated
#   evidence and were found only by hand. Prose did not prevent it; a
#   deterministic inventory the audit enumerates against does.
# - Report-only (WARN class): a non-canonical entry never flips the audit
#   verdict or an exit code.

# --- directories -------------------------------------------------------------
archive
briefs
friction
live
locks
loop
reports
reviews
tdd
